  <p class="source-doc-note"><em>"Please Go to Hell" names Charles (Charlie) Slaght and Woody Wintz, and its "Dedication" poem closes with the two of them together; this caption calls him "Woodrow," which matches the full name the site's family research gives for Woody. The Name Index also records that the mine engineer Paul Davis, John's geology teacher, married Edith Wintz, a sister of Woody's. If the Paul Davis of this caption is that man, two of the four are brothers-in-law; the book does not say so. Ed McCargish was one of the Amethyst Mine's hoistmen, according to <a href="/writings/please-go-to-hell/dedication-and-the-amethyst-crew-1947/">"Please Go to Hell."</a> The two verses are printed on separate pages, one under each photograph.</em></p>
